source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Dissolve groups: their objects stay where they are, in the group's frame if it stood in one. The groups are the linked object and every --object.
A group left with fewer than 2 objects by `o rm` dissolves by itself. It prints one line per changed object with @N and its link.

USAGE
  holst object ungroup <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name

FLAGS
      --object object   A group, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o ungroup "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4
  $ holst o ungroup "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
